{
  "schema": "rea-viral/words@1",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "about": [
    "The word lists text_probe.py and draft_check.py use to read a post's words. One file, so the lists can be extended and translated.",
    "Covered today: English only. A post in any other language gets every word-based feature as unknown (null), never a guess. Features that need no words (lengths, lines, numbers, question marks, emoji, hashtags, links, mentions) are measured in every language.",
    "To add a language: copy the en block under its code (es, pt, de ...), translate every list, and keep the same keys. 'detect' must hold words that are common in that language and rare in the others (so the English list leaves out do, an, on, or, so, for and was); a post is taken as that language when at least 2 of its words, and at least 20% of them, are in the list, or 1 word and 20% in a post under 8 words, or when the network tags the post with that language.",
    "Matching: lower case, whole words, straight and curly apostrophes treated alike. In 'asks', '*' stands for any one word, and a phrase ending in '*' needs a word there."
  ],
  "languages": {
    "en": {
      "name": "English",
      "detect": ["the", "and", "of", "to", "is", "are", "were", "you", "your", "that", "this", "with", "have", "has",
                 "what", "how", "why", "they", "their", "we", "our", "be", "been", "will", "would", "can", "just", "not",
                 "don't", "it's", "i'm", "from", "about", "if", "when", "which", "who", "more", "than", "there", "here",
                 "all", "get", "it", "my", "at", "but", "by", "people", "should", "these", "those", "because",
                 "could", "into", "out", "up", "one", "every", "most", "only", "now", "like", "make", "want", "need"],
      "you": ["you", "your", "you're", "yours", "yourself", "yourselves", "you've", "you'll", "you'd"],
      "i": ["i", "i'm", "i've", "i'll", "i'd", "me", "my", "mine", "myself"],
      "we": ["we", "we're", "we've", "we'll", "we'd", "us", "our", "ours", "ourselves"],
      "negation_openers": ["stop", "don't", "dont", "never", "no", "nobody", "nothing", "not", "quit", "avoid", "forget",
                           "none", "nor", "can't", "won't", "isn't", "aren't", "doesn't", "didn't", "wasn't",
